# Photographs a shop took of its own products. The shop's, not the repo's --
# and carried by pos:backup, which is where they belong.
#
# The folder itself is kept, though, because it is not only somewhere to put
# files: deploy/update.sh chmods it so www-data may write there, and a chmod on
# a path that does not exist fails -- which under `set -e` ends the deploy one
# step before PHP-FPM is reloaded. Ignoring the contents and tracking the
# directory is what stops a fresh checkout from arriving without it.
/public/uploads/*
!/public/uploads/.gitkeep
/storage/*.key
/storage/pail
/vendor
Homestead.json
Homestead.yaml
Thumbs.db

# The register keeps its sales in SQLite -- never commit live data.
/database/*.sqlite
/database/*.sqlite-journal
/database/*.sqlite-shm
/database/*.sqlite-wal
